# Review routing. The last matching pattern wins, so the specific entries below
# the default are the ones that decide.
#
# @aj3x is the only maintainer today, so every line names the same person and
# nothing here gates anything yet. It is written anyway because the code is now
# 100+ files: when a second contributor arrives, the question "who should look
# at this?" has to have an answer that does not depend on recognising a path.
# The specific entries are not ceremony — each one is a place where a change
# that looks harmless, lints clean and leaves the suite green can still do real
# damage.

*                           @aj3x

# Saved-state shape and its migrations. migrate() runs on every load of every
# returning user's data; a wrong step here rewrites real projects with no error
# anywhere, and the damage is already on disk by the time anyone notices.
# S is also reassigned wholesale (setS), so its module is the one place the
# whole state object is defined.
/src/core/state.js          @aj3x
/src/core/migrate.js        @aj3x

# The 24 design tokens. They must stay CSS custom properties: dark mode works
# by re-declaring them under @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark), so converting
# one to a Sass $variable silently deletes dark mode with every test green.
/src/styles/_tokens.scss    @aj3x

# Import/export is the only path a user's data leaves and re-enters the app by,
# and the collision rules decide whether a merge keeps or overwrites their work.
/src/io/                    @aj3x

# CI, Pages deployment and this file. A bad change here can publish the wrong
# thing to the live site, or quietly stop running the gate.
/.github/                   @aj3x

# The suite is capped at 20% of the codebase (ideally under 10%, it is at
# 9.98%). Additions need an argument about what they catch, and deletions need
# to be distinguished from removing scaffolding that has finished its job —
# both are review questions, not mechanical ones. See test/README.md.
/test/                      @aj3x

# The build is what makes the one-file deployment model work: the include
# plugin, the classic script tag and the singlefile inlining are load-bearing.
/vite.config.js             @aj3x
